1058	    /**
1059	     * Finds the first existing owner that already carries the given comparison {@code key}, derived
1060	     * from each owner by {@code keyExtractor}. Owners for which the extractor yields {@code null} are
1061	     * ignored (a {@code null} key never equals the sought key). The create endpoint's duplicate
1062	     * checks reduce both an existing owner and the owner being created to the same canonical key;
1063	     * this returns the matched existing owner itself, so a caller can either reject the collision or
1064	     * record which owner was matched. Owners flagged deleted (soft-deleted) are excluded, so a
1065	     * collision with only a deleted owner is not reported and the create is allowed.
1066	     *
1067	     * @param keyExtractor derives an owner's canonical comparison key (may return {@code null})
1068	     * @param key the canonical key of the owner being created
1069	     * @return the first existing owner sharing the key, or empty when none does
1070	     */
1071	    private Optional<Owner> findExistingOwner(Function<Owner, String> keyExtractor, String key) {
1072	        return this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
1073	            .filter(owner -> !owner.isDeleted())
1074	            .filter(owner -> key.equals(keyExtractor.apply(owner)))
1075	            .findFirst();
1076	    }
